sentences.l:
and having come out, down he sat upon the polished stones,
which for him were before the high doors,
white, glistening with oil;

But when they had prayed and had thrown forward the barley-for-sprinkling,
at once Nestor’s son, high-spirited Thrasymedes,
struck, standing close;

But when she had bathed him and anointed him richly with oil,
and about him a fine cloak had thrown and a tunic,
out of the bath he stepped, in body like the immortals;
